<title>NETHERLANDS: Hagemeyer proposes two for one share split.</title>
<headline>Hagemeyer proposes two for one share split.</headline>
<dateline>NAARDEN, Netherlands 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading company Hagemeyer NV said it will propose a two for one share split to its annual meeting of shareholders on April 17.</p>
<p>The firm earlier announced a 1996 net profit of 285.2 million guilders, up 47.5 percent from 1996's 193.3 million.</p>
<p>Hagemeyer, in which Hong Kong's First Pacific Co has a controlling stake, will pay a dividend of 2.28 guilders, 0.75 of which has already been paid. The final payment of 1.53 can be taken up in cash or as an optional stock dividend. Details of the payment in shares will be given in April.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
